{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/188955-time-to-borrow-npc-and-pcs","id":188955,"title":"Time to Borrow NPC! and PCs!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-05T16:30:26-07:00","id":188955,"title":"Time to Borrow NPC! and PCs!","content":"im starting a game set on New York City, theres a lot of elements i want to tacle, both heroes and villians, and other parties involved within the city (set in 99') but i feel like NY is lacking characters..so i made this thread so you can share your characters for others to use and viseeversa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T16:43:49-07:00","id":189698,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing that this is an <b>Aberrant</b> game?<br /> <br /> If so, I figure the <b>Year One</b> section is meant as a &quot;tourist&quot; guide for a globetrotting game, and to emphasise that other places like Ibiza and Mumbai are more Nova-rich to make it stand out from the NY-centric Marvel universe and DC's Gotham and Metropolis. But as a city of millions and an economic and cultural centre, it would have its share of excitement. I'd look at how the city is portrayed outside of the superhero genre - crime drama, big business, the entertainment industry and so on.<br /> <br /> Who protects Wall Street from super-hackers? Their own super-Sysops, a Nova-constructed AI, or keeping everything off the OpNet - so Nova &quot;traditional&quot; thieves and Elite security fight over it physically?<br /> <br /> What's the hottest club, Nova or baseline? (I'd be tempted to recycle an idea from <b>New York By Night</b> here, with a Teragen cell based on of the Sabbat pack moving among the city's young social elite and nudging them to more 'inhuman' kinds of decadent entertainment.)<br /> <br /> Who apart from Buendia has Nova models at Fashion Week? <b>Aberrant</b> characters are often celebrities unless they actively avoid it, so they could get into all the VIP parties and see the politicking and sniping up close and personal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T17:51:17-07:00","id":189725,"title":"","content":"Aberrant has the obvious <s>Batman</s> Gothic Knight as New York's municipal defender.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T15:20:17-07:00","id":191726,"title":"","content":"Have you ever heard of the guy named Blackwolf? He's a pretty awesome guy in NYC; had something of a breakdown many, many years ago, and he put himself back together as &quot;Blackwolf the Dragonmaster&quot;. I actually included him as a Mesmerist in my Aberrant game; he doesn't do much in terms of &quot;going out and being a badass hero&quot;, but he's <i>there</i>, and adds a bit of flavor to the game -- he's human, he has feelings, he has a life. He can be hurt, he can be happy. It's just one of those things which helps to make the game and the world feel more alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T17:20:17-07:00","id":191841,"title":"","content":"So we have, The Avatar (erupted 1999), Enriche Meludos (erupted 1998), Fireman (erupted 1998), Gothic Knight (erupted before 2013... no certain date), Lydia Divine (before 2007), and Percy Andreesen (erupted before 2008) as canon New Yorkers. There other visitors, but they claim NY, NY as home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T18:13:38-07:00","id":191872,"title":"","content":"For NPCs, I have one that I made for the same campaign of mine. It is a very long-running campaign, and one that ran through all three settings. There's one NPC who lives in NYC with the party; he's a very old Daredevil, who's been through both World Wars and also the Vietnam War. He's one of the best pilots and drivers in the world, and a damn good soldier/killer, but he's world weary from so much violence and living so long. His name is Maxwell Denton, usually goes by his last name (in fact, he goes by it so often, that many PCs honestly believed his first name was &quot;Denton&quot; until he politely introduced himself to a Utopian NPC).<br /> <br /> As a resulting combination of Ability Mastery (Savvy), a few Knacks, and good genre-savvy humor on our part, it is a running joke that Denton is personally known in every bar or questionable den of iniquity in the world; the joke being he's globe-trotted so much, and drank so much, that he's already been drinking everywhere. Denton also has a comically terrible sense of other people when it comes to members of the opposite sex, and as such always winds up with the craziest or most unbalanced person in the area. He has a habit of marrying someone, then growing to despise them (the feeling is always mutual), and getting a divorce. His primary means of getting away from his ever-growing list of exes is to simply outlive them, and in the meantime don't let them find out his new address.<br /> <br /> John Hurt's portrayal of The Doctor turned out to be an excellent example of how this character acts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For PCs (who would likely be NPCs in your game), there's one that I made for a game a long time ago (and wound up running as an NPC in my game) by the name of Sean Kelley. He is a Nova, and one who would have erupted very recently in your timeline. He was the sole survivor of a rather fiery plane crash, and only survived due to his eruption. His schtick is that he has Mega-Stamina 5 (with Adaptability) and Armor 5, with the Impervious Extra. With a combination of Mega-Stamina Enhancements and a few Body Modifications, he has a phenomenal number of Health Levels. Unfortunately, because this was made as a starting character, he has developed an equally phenomenal amount of Taint as a result of such an instantaneous accrual of power. His Taint and Aberrations manifest as extreme physical changes to his body; he, essentially, looks like a giant, 8-foot-tall alligator man. He also suffers from the &quot;Permanent Power&quot; Aberration, and cannot turn off his Armor. Adding insult to injury, Sean has no dots in Dormancy, and cannot &quot;dorm down&quot; to become baseline and remove, even temporarily, his problems.<br /> <br /> Despite what is commonly reported on N!, Sean is not from Louisiana; he is from the Midwest. He does not go by the Nova name &quot;Alligator Boy&quot;, he goes by his <i>actual name</i>, thank-you-very-much. He knows very little about fighting, or shooting, or breathing fire, or doing anything cool like that; he's a mechanical engineer, and not even a very good one at that (very average: Intelligence 2, Engineering 2, with a specialty in Mechanics; he got his degree, then got a job which covered his costs of living). In time, he will join the DeVries Agency as an Elite who can be called in to clean up or repair things in dangerous conditions (such as the reactor core of a nuclear power plant).<br /> <br /> Sean has a secret shame and sense of survivor's guilt. While the few times he grudgingly speaks about the accident, he describes immediately trying to find and help survivors, this is in fact a fabrication. When the plane crashed, he panicked and ran out of the flames; it took him several moments to realize that he had even erupted, and that he was completely unharmed. By the time he ran back in to the wreckage, everyone was dead. In reality, the crash was too violent for anyone else to have survived, even had he taken immediate action. Sean still feels guilt over his gross delay, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T23:50:00-07:00","id":192111,"title":"","content":"I read Planetary time ago and i really liked it, specially the whole Fourth Man thing. ever since i been tempted to use them on my aberrant game, but im not sure how to translate them into game. Would they be Proterus? Teragen?.<br /> <br /> Also i would like some thoughts on something i made time ago. My players were fighting the nazi threat during WW2 and i throw at them a cultist character of an Eldritch horror, this guy could control flames (thanks to a suit) and he ended up being throwed into a portal and vanished -the players thought he died-<br /> <br /> im taking a lot of influence by both DC and Marvel (but mainly DC) on my game, Do you think i should go all Secret Origins/Starro/The Center or all Avengers Vs Loki on the movie and make this guy come back with an army of eldritch horrors at his command?. I know this would be a game changer, specially since after this i want to run the canon events of the world books I and II. any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}